title: 'transaction-pool: resubmit retracted transactions to existing views'
doc:
- audience: Node Dev
  description: |-
    Fixes two cases in the fork-aware transaction pool where transactions could get lost or never
    be reported as finalized:

    - When a re-org (or finalization) enacted a block that already had a view, the transactions
      from the retracted blocks were not resubmitted to that view. Transactions only known from
      the retracted block bodies were lost for this view and all views built on top of it. This
      became more likely since views are created for every imported block. The transactions from
      the retracted blocks are now resubmitted to the existing view.
    - A late `NewBlock` notification for an old fork block could cause the maintenance of a
      following `Finalized` event to be skipped (tree route longer than the skip threshold). In
      that case transactions in the finalized blocks never received the `Finalized` event and
      were not purged from the mempool. Finalization is now never skipped.
crates:
- name: sc-transaction-pool
  bump: patch
